@page "/{*path:nonfile}"

@*
    Two jobs, one per host.

    In the browser host it is never rendered: Root.razor has no <Routes/> for a
    matched page to land in. It exists so ASP.NET endpoint routing has a routable
    component for every non-file URL, which is what makes the server answer /logs,
    /host-changer and friends with the Root shell — the App component's own Router,
    running as an interactive island, then resolves the actual page.

    In the WinForms host it is a real page, because App.razor's Router scans this
    assembly and a catch-all matches anything unrouted. That would otherwise
    swallow the Router's <NotFound> and render a blank page, so it says the same
    thing NotFound did.
*@

<PageTitle>Not found</PageTitle>
<p role="alert">Sorry, there's nothing at this address.</p>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Path { get; set; }
}
